@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@
+---
+import TenderHubLayout from "../../layouts/TenderHubLayout.astro";
+---
+
+<TenderHubLayout
+  title="Western Cape Government Tenders"
+  description="Tender opportunities across Western Cape provincial departments, the City of Cape Town, and district municipalities from Drakenstein to Mossel Bay."
+  hubType="Province"
+  hubName="Western Cape"
+  contextLabel="the Western Cape"
+  lastUpdated="2026-05-14"
+>
+  <h2>About procurement in the Western Cape</h2>
+  <p>
+    The Western Cape consistently posts the cleanest audit outcomes of any province, which means tighter
+    compliance enforcement on bidders too. The province's procurement spans transversal term contracts,
+    one-off infrastructure tenders, and a substantial municipal pipeline anchored by the City of Cape Town —
+    one of the largest single procuring entities in South Africa outside the national departments.
+  </p>
+
+  <h2>Key procuring entities</h2>
+
+  <h3>Provincial departments</h3>
+  <ul>
+    <li><strong>Western Cape Department of Health and Wellness</strong> — Tygerberg, Groote Schuur, and district hospital upgrades; pharmaceuticals; clinic builds in Khayelitsha and Mitchells Plain.</li>
+    <li><strong>Western Cape Education Department (WCED)</strong> — school construction, sanitation, e-learning devices, scholar transport, often via panel contracts.</li>
+    <li><strong>Department of Transport and Public Works</strong> — N1, N2, and rural corridor maintenance; provincial building works.</li>
+    <li><strong>Department of Human Settlements</strong> — well-located mixed-income housing projects with subcontracting goals.</li>
+    <li><strong>Department of Agriculture</strong> — fresh produce market upgrades, cold-chain infrastructure, irrigation.</li>
+  </ul>
+
+  <h3>Municipalities</h3>
+  <ul>
+    <li><strong>City of Cape Town</strong> — water resilience, sanitation, electricity, refuse, MyCiTi expansion, ICT systems.</li>
+    <li><strong>Stellenbosch, Drakenstein, Mossel Bay, George</strong> — embedded generation programmes and local infrastructure.</li>
+    <li>The five district municipalities (Cape Winelands, Central Karoo, Garden Route, Overberg, West Coast) and their constituent local municipalities run their own SCM units.</li>
+  </ul>
+
+  <h2>Where Western Cape tenders are advertised</h2>
+  <p>
+    All provincial and municipal tenders appear on the
+    <a href="https://www.etenders.gov.za" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">eTenders Publication Portal</a>.
+    The Western Cape Provincial Treasury also publishes a
+    <a href="https://www.westerncape.gov.za/general-publication/western-cape-government-tender-bulletin" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">weekly tender bulletin</a>,
+    and the City of Cape Town runs its own
+    <a href="https://www.capetown.gov.za" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">supplier portal</a>.
+  </p>
+
+  <h2>What sets the Western Cape apart</h2>
+  <p>
+    Three factors shape the bidding environment here. First, the province's <strong>Energy Resilience Programme</strong>
+    has unlocked a steady pipeline of solar PV, battery storage, and energy management tenders at government buildings.
+    Second, the <strong>City of Cape Town's water resilience plan</strong> drives continuous tenders for leak detection,
+    pipe replacement, and treatment works. Third, the province's emphasis on
+    <strong>local content and B-BBEE specific goals</strong> means bidders should ensure documentation is current
+    and consortium arrangements are in place well before adverts go out.
+  </p>
+
+  <h2>Bidding strategy</h2>
+  <ul>
+    <li>Get on the WCED transversal term contracts early — these panel contracts run for multi-year periods.</li>
+    <li>Verify your CSD commodity codes match the sectors you serve; the province's evaluators check carefully.</li>
+    <li>Attend Provincial Treasury Supplier Development Unit information sessions.</li>
+  </ul>
+
+  <p>
+    Read our <a href="/blog/western-cape-tender-opportunities-2026">2026 Western Cape outlook</a> for the
+    detailed sector pipeline.
+  </p>
+</TenderHubLayout>
